## 5. Resolve setup errors

| Symptom | Next action |
|---|---|
| Command not found | Check installation location, shell file, and PATH. Open a new terminal before trying again. |
| Certificate or registry authentication failure | Check required VPN, registry permission, and runtime-specific enterprise trust configuration. Keep TLS verification enabled. |
| Gradle Java compatibility error | Compare the wrapper, Android Gradle Plugin, IDE JDK, terminal Java, and daemon JVM configuration. Preserve the wrapper and locks. |
| Missing SDK package or license | Install the exact required package and review its license in SDK Manager. |
| Emulator or Simulator will not boot | Check selected runtime, supported host OS, architecture, free space, and the specific error. Avoid an unrelated tool upgrade or data reset. |
| `xcodebuild` requires Xcode or first-launch setup | Check `xcode-select -p`, open the selected Xcode, and finish its required setup. |
| Ruby or Node architecture mismatch | Confirm a native ARM64 terminal and the selected runtime installation. Resolve mixed runtime paths before reinstalling dependencies. |
| Missing approved version or installation method | Ask the application owner or [Teams Support](../../support/support.mdx). Do not invent a project configuration. |

Share the failing step, relevant versions, and a sanitized error excerpt when requesting help. Do not post complete environment dumps or credential files.

**Next:** [First Local Run](../first-local-run.mdx) — clone the assigned source, install its locked dependencies, and build an actual application. Tool verification here does not establish that the application builds or is released.




